Event loop tests
================

Behaviour tests for QEventLoop: timers, posted events, socket notifiers,
nested loops, cross-thread wake-ups, X11 event handling and the
coexistence with GLib sources (GDBus, g_idle_add, g_main_loop_run,
GTask, libpulse's GLib main loop). They were written to compare the
stock select() loop with the GLib based loop (configure -glib-eventloop)
and are not part of the normal build ("make" does not touch this
directory; there is no .pro file on purpose).

Build against the library of this source tree (configure + make first),
or against another tree with QTDIR=...:

    tests/eventloop/build.sh               # binaries in tests/eventloop/build
    tests/eventloop/build.sh -asan         # with -fsanitize=address,undefined
    QTDIR=/other/qt tests/eventloop/build.sh tests/eventloop/build-other

Run everything (the GUI checks only if $DISPLAY is set):

    tests/eventloop/run.sh [builddir]

or single programs:

    looptest                 the main suite (non-GUI)
    looptest gui             the main suite plus the X11 checks; opens a few
                             small windows that close by themselves
    looptest recreate [gui]  QApplication destroyed, the GLib main context
                             iterated, a new QApplication created (3 rounds)
    looptest early [gui]     QEventLoop created before the QApplication
    looptest cpu [s [gui]]   CPU used by a 10 ms QTimer (getrusage)
    t2                       GLib main context iterated after ~QApplication

looptest prints one PASS/FAIL/SKIP line per check and exits with 1 if a
check failed. Checks that need the GLib loop (GLib and GDBus sources,
notifiers on fds above FD_SETSIZE, ...) are reported as SKIP when the
library was built without QT_GLIB_EVENTLOOP; the stock loop must pass
all the others.

Needs: g++, pkg-config, GLib/GIO development files (gio-2.0), libX11,
a D-Bus session bus for the GDBus checks and, optionally,
libpulse-mainloop-glib with a running PulseAudio/PipeWire server.

Note: <gio/gio.h> (and other GObject headers) must be included before
the Qt headers, because Qt 3 #defines "signals" and GDBusInterfaceInfo
has a member of that name.
